# route: level=w9_l2_coop difficulty=expert players=2 ends=exit after=level:w9_l2b_coop expect=wipes:0,x2_gates:2,min_checkpoints:5
# The two-stream Expert route of The Roc's Spire in co-op (designer D9a; recorded from closed-loop macros,
# build/d9a/bot_w9_l2_coop.gd; re-recorded by enemies-A for the heavy-keeper ruling of G3 with
# build/enemies_a10/bot_w9_l2_coop_ea.gd, P1|P2): the gust gaps in the lulls, the drop clouds one hero at a time,
# gate 'brace' (the Bull Rex wakes and charges; while it is still 100 px off both step down from the mouth into
# the sunken hall and crouch side by side 8 px apart: the Brace Wall stops it dead, and both strike its dazed
# head - the first strike, charged by the crouch, takes its 25 hp; its back counts for nobody), the cloud
# hall's tribesman and Roller (P2 jumps the first valley gap once P1 left its landing), gate 'drive' (P2 curls
# at the edge, P1 charges and bats him across; P2's latch plate sinks the slab bridge).
# Re-recorded in wf11 (levels; build/levels/bot_w9_l2_coop.gd, the same bot with the gate's new columns) on the
# rebuilt 'drive': 13 cells of tar (DESIGN G79, the gust jump), so P1 holds a full crouch charge before he bats
# P2 across; the latch plate (219-220) sinks the slab over the first 9 cells and P1 hops the last 4 in a lull.
# The cloud hall's Roller is left out of the co-op file (it rolled into the batter at the lip).
